The Zstandard generated-frame tests invoke the unmodified decodecorpus tool
from Zstandard 1.5.7 and compare its paired frame and plaintext outputs with
Arkivo and the native reference decoder. Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc.
and affiliates. The verified source download retains LICENSE and COPYING;
these tests use the BSD license option. Native code is used only for testing.
The dictionary regression reads the invalidRepCode byte array directly from
the verified tests/invalidDictionaries.c source; it does not execute that file.
The seekable tests adapt the five scenarios in contrib/seekable_format/tests/
seekable_tests.c and finite parameter cases from tests/fuzz/seekable_roundtrip.c
under the same BSD license option, retaining the reference sources and notices.
Streaming regressions adapt zstreamtest.c's raw-block progress, source-size,
context-reuse, empty-buffer, dictionary lifecycle and parameter matrices,
repeated-table cases, and embedded historical sequence cases. Hash-selected
round trips adapt roundTripCrash.c, including its worker configuration.
Finite fuzz regressions adapt tests/fuzz/decompress_cross_format.c,
decompress_dstSize_tooSmall.c, simple_decompress.c, stream_decompress.c,
zstd_frame_info.c and fuzz_data_producer.c's input interpretation. Basic tests
adapt fuzzer.c's input-extent, skippable-size and checksum regressions.
These tests use the same BSD license option.
Compression-capacity tests adapt tests/fuzz/simple_compress.c's input
partition and parameter order, retaining native destination-too-small
checks and adding Java buffer guards, incremental completion and reset.
Round-trip tests invoke the unmodified tests/fuzz/simple_round_trip.c
assertions with a test-only adapter under the same BSD license option.
The adapter exports frames and parameters for Java interoperability tests,
retaining native determinism, parameter rollback and overlapping decoding.
Reused inputs clear a stale decoder maximum-block restriction; a separate
native/Java regression checks that restriction and subsequent recovery.
Streaming round-trip tests observe tests/fuzz/stream_round_trip.c's original
operation loop, parameter selection and overlapping-decompression assertions
under the same BSD license option. Its accepted chunks and completed actions
are replayed through Java encoders; both decoders verify plaintext visibility
at every completed flush and frame end without reading later encoded bytes.
Dictionary-loading tests invoke tests/fuzz/dictionary_loader.c's original
assertions under the same BSD license option, retaining its tail parameters,
same-bytes dictionary/source inputs and native loading modes. Java tests
verify copied dictionary ownership, reset and bidirectional interoperability,
distinguishing Java's short-dictionary and zero-identifier preconditions.
Raw-history tests observe tests/fuzz/raw_dictionary_round_trip.c under the
same BSD license option, retaining independent source/dictionary partitioning,
reduced output capacity, loading modes and the original round-trip assertions.
Fresh and retained native contexts provide frames for Java interoperability.
Trained-dictionary tests observe tests/fuzz/dictionary_round_trip.c under
the same BSD license option, preserving FUZZ_train's sample selection,
training failures, parameter rollback and repeated-compression assertions.
Exported dictionaries and frames are checked in both interoperability directions.
Dictionary-decoding tests observe tests/fuzz/dictionary_decompress.c under
the same BSD license option, retaining original training, prepared/loaded/prefix
branches and output capacities. Java checks native successful output, bounded
rejection, unchanged input, output guards and decoder recovery after reset.
FSE tests adapt tests/fuzz/fse_read_ncount.c's signed normalized frequencies
and trailing-byte generation. A separately built test-only adapter invokes
the verified native FSE reader, writer and table builder to check signed
counts, descriptions and decoding states independently of the Java code.
Huffman tests adapt tests/fuzz/huf_round_trip.c and huf_decompress.c. The
test-only native Huffman generator preserves the upstream parameter layout,
capacity handling and round-trip assertions, and exports tables and streams
for independent Java decoding. See LICENSES/Zstd-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
Block tests adapt tests/fuzz/block_round_trip.c and block_decompress.c under
the same BSD license option. Their test-only native adapter retains the
prefix partition, compression levels, source-size cap, output capacities
and context reset rules, and exchanges raw compressed blocks with Java.
Prefix tests adapt zstreamtest.c's full and raw prefix lifetimes under the
same BSD license option. The native adapter checks prefix consumption and
subsequent independent frames, including decoding frames produced by Java.

